Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.88,0:00:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Back up!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.92,0:00:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep going!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.48,0:00:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is it that you sense nearby weather?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.20,0:00:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying that Jolyne's\Nthe one who's near the hospital?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.56,0:00:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Or do you mean the priest is\Nthe person that's already here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.84,0:00:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, I can sense\Nthree people, Anastasia.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.40,0:00:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene is one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.74,0:00:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The priest is here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.20,0:00:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But there is somebody else.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.04,0:00:35.32,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta find them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.44,0:00:36.36,Default,,0,0,0,,But where are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.44,0:00:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Could they be inside\None of these buildings?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.06,0:00:44.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, ladies. Welcome\Naboard. Unfortunately,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.44,0:00:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,this plane is expected\Nto lose control and crash
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.46,0:00:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,into the ground at approximately\N21.33 on July Saudi, 2005.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.08,0:00:57.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.70,0:00:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think you're doing, Jolene?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.14,0:01:01.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not planning on\Nopening that door, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.34,0:01:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I wasn't able to find\Nthe exit on the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.72,0:01:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,So the fastest way to end this is to find\Nthe stand user and attack him directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.62,0:01:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Hermes, hold on tight to my rope again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.84,0:01:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And strap yourself in somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.90,0:01:15.70,Default,,0,0,0,,And you, flight attendant lady,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.78,0:01:19.18,Default,,0,0,0,,switch the settings on this door\Nso that I can open it manually.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.26,0:01:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Yo, hang on.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.50,0:01:23.82,Default,,0,0,0,,It ain't exactly a good idea to open\Nthe door when the plane's still moving,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.90,0:01:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.81,0:01:25.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The air pressure would...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.73,0:01:26.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.20,0:01:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Nah, never mind!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.98,0:01:32.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Go for it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.46,0:01:36.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Use the air pressure to slam\Ninto those motherfuckers!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.08,0:01:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Mayday, mayday!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.48,0:01:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like we just got hit by a damn MiG!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.04,0:01:49.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I've lost all control!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.74,0:01:52.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess finishing them will\Nbe easier than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.90,0:01:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.56,0:01:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyway, I think the back of\Nthe plane took a serious hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.28,0:02:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you go check out\Nhow bad the damage is?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.80,0:02:02.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.70,0:02:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.70,0:02:18.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.84,0:02:20.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Stone Ocean!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.26,0:02:24.98,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Officer McCoy here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.66,0:02:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We just arrived at the scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.30,0:02:28.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Not sure what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.80,0:02:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't tell how deep it is from the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.30,0:02:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,surface, but there's a large hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.14,0:02:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,As I told you, Jolene Kujo's\Nskills were sharpened in prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.96,0:02:39.82,Default,,0,0,0,,She already anticipated\Nwhat could happen in
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.90,0:02:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,the event that her initial\Nattack was a failure.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.60,0:02:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Clearly, this is why she\Ngot out of the airplane.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.18,0:02:49.28,Default,,0,0,0,,She was waiting for the police to arrive,\Nso that they would use their radio,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.36,0:02:51.14,Default,,0,0,0,,giving her a chance to grab it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.22,0:02:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now she can contact her Allies\Ndepending on frequency range that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.98,0:02:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,radio can be used to call cell phones\Nas well shut the Fuck up already
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.76,0:03:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,enough does it look like I'm\Nlosing here huh answer me father
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.46,0:03:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,poochie I'm Still winning this damn\Nbattle aren't I destiny is mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.72,0:03:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.88,0:04:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for watching.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.42,0:04:23.60,Default,,0,0,0,,In the end of the day,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.68,0:04:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,it's the end of the day of my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.50,0:04:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't have any cash, so it was\Nonly going to be for a few days,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.54,0:04:57.72,Default,,0,0,0,,but as I was looking for a\Nplace to spend the night,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.80,0:05:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,a pair of spiked shoes\Ncame falling from the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.16,0:05:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,They were baseball spikes, and\Nthey had a real nice smell.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.04,0:05:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I looked up to see if someone\Nthrew them from the building above,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.10,0:05:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,but they looked so new.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.36,0:05:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,The shoe size was 28\Nand a half centimeters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.56,0:05:15.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Though they were way too big for me,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.48,0:05:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I liked the clacking sound the spikes\Nmade when I walked down the street,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.42,0:05:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,so I decided to keep them on for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.66,0:05:24.72,Default,,0,0,0,,It wasn't long until some\Ncops came and arrested me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.28,0:05:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,This hearing today is not a formal trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.14,0:05:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,We just want to ask some questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.50,0:05:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.74,0:05:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you steal those\Nshoes you were wearing?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.96,0:05:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Turns out,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.87,0:05:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,those spikes were signed by the\Nfamous baseball player Ichiro
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.60,0:05:42.95,Default,,0,0,0,,and donated to a facility for\Nchildren with disabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.70,0:05:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,If you sold them to a collector, they\Nwould have gone as high as ten grand.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.42,0:05:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,So everybody wanted to\Nget their hands on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.26,0:05:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Like a dumb kid, I told the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.84,0:05:54.78,Default,,0,0,0,,They came falling out of the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.04,0:05:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You should be ashamed of yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.62,0:05:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you steal from\Nchildren less fortunate!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.08,0:06:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You need to be straightened out!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.68,0:06:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Go spend some time in the\Njuvenile detention facility!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.82,0:06:05.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The judge found me\Nguilty on circumstantial
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.02,0:06:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,evidence and sentenced me\Nto six months in juvie.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.54,0:06:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And even my parents agreed to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.46,0:06:14.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Four months later, the\Nactual culprit confessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.10,0:06:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Since Ichiro's spikes were so famous,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.14,0:06:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,the thief knew they'd be found and threw\Nthem in an air vent to be rid of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.42,0:06:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And somehow, they ended up\Noutside of the building.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.94,0:06:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,By the time it was discovered\Nthat I was wrongly condemned,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.92,0:06:30.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I was already crippled in mind and body,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.22,0:06:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,to the point where I was too\Nweak to even walk straight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.54,0:06:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,One day, I fell into a\Nrandom hole in the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.28,0:06:37.11,Default,,0,0,0,,In the moment,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.19,0:06:40.05,Default,,0,0,0,,all I could think about was breaking\Nmy fall by extending my hand out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.14,0:06:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's when I saw a knife in a\Nplastic bag that had been buried there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.48,0:06:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It went right through my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.36,0:06:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think you're\Ndoing causing me trouble, kid?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.24,0:06:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I was hiding that knife\Nthere for a reason, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.06,0:06:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The next day, a guy three years\Nolder than me kicked my ass.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.48,0:06:57.28,Default,,0,0,0,,He was a gangster's little\Nbitch that did his dirty work.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.36,0:06:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though my hand was\Ntreated by a doctor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.66,0:07:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,two weeks later my wound\Nwas still expelling pus?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.10,0:07:04.46,Default,,0,0,0,,and worms even started crawling out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.54,0:07:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,After that, I nearly\Ndied from a high fever.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.26,0:07:09.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Since then, I've tried to live\Na bitter life of solitude,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.00,0:07:13.12,Default,,0,0,0,,keeping away from the public\Neye as much as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.48,0:07:16.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Then one day, when I was taken\Nto piss by some garbage cans,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.86,0:07:18.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the wall started to\Ncrumble and revealed the
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.80,0:07:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,skeletal remains of a\Nwoman who died years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.76,0:07:23.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, after all this time,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.20,0:07:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,the reason why my life has been so utterly\Nfucked up is finally crystal clear to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.72,0:07:30.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.76,0:07:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Netherworld!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.42,0:07:33.28,Default,,0,0,0,,But still,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.60,0:07:35.72,Default,,0,0,0,,just because I can control my power now,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.80,0:07:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,am I really supposed to\Nbe grateful to Father
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.78,0:07:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Pucci for helping me\Nrealize my full potential?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.80,0:07:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell no.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.92,0:07:46.45,Default,,0,0,0,,The blood that's been running through\Nmy veins all along is Dio's, my father.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.14,0:07:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Priest, do you honestly believe\Nyou're that important to all of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.44,0:07:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you not think that I would throw\Nyour ass onto that plane as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.30,0:07:56.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't even failed yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.18,0:07:58.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't done anything wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.48,0:08:03.48,Default,,0,0,0,,He's just like that old bitch of a\Njudge who only values her own opinion.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.56,0:08:07.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm really starting to lose my\Npatience with this so-called holy man.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.80,0:08:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I am the one who's invincible here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.04,0:08:12.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything is possible if I use Netherworld!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.70,0:08:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is he the only one?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.74,0:08:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,On the new moon, maybe it should\Nbe me who comes out on top.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.92,0:08:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I'm the one who acquires Dio's\Npower instead, and not that damn priest?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.78,0:08:33.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I have every right to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.54,0:08:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, I am Dio's son.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.54,0:08:40.66,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Weather Forecast's memory disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.18,0:08:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, maybe this can be used\Nto put things in my favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.98,0:08:48.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The only one who gets to\Nattain heaven should be me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.00,0:08:49.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.00,0:08:55.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Emporio!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.40,0:08:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Pick up the phone!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.64,0:08:59.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Emporio! Hey, Mr. Pilot!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.64,0:09:01.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of jet fighter is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.38,0:09:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And how the hell do I get out of here?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.32,0:09:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,There's got to be some way to break\Nloose, even if I'm still sitting down!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.46,0:09:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I've seen it in lots of movies!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.12,0:09:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry the fuck up and tell me how!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.36,0:09:13.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The seat has a lever you\Ncan pull to eject yourself,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.32,0:09:16.20,Default,,0,0,0,,but in my case, I never\Ngot the chance to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.76,0:09:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My jet hit the ground before\NI was able to pull it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.50,0:09:20.66,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.88,0:09:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why nobody's gonna be\Ngetting off this aircraft.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.78,0:09:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It's already too late to pull\Nthe ejection lever in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.10,0:09:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.54,0:09:32.60,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing calling so soon?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.72,0:09:33.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, Emporio!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.50,0:09:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.41,0:09:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now we're in a big\Nhole in the hospital floor,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.22,0:09:39.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and Hermes is riding on a\Nplane that's gonna crash!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.84,0:09:42.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm in a fighter jet\Nthat's also about to crash!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.40,0:09:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Find a way for us to get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.40,0:09:46.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.68,0:09:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Father Poochie, do we need\NJolene's body intact after this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.62,0:09:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They weren't able to\Nretrieve all of the jet
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.58,0:09:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,fighter pilot's remains\Nafter the jet crashed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.30,0:09:58.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, he was blown to bits.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.68,0:10:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, just calm down, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.34,0:10:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand what\Nyou're saying at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.26,0:10:06.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll head back to the hospital right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.26,0:10:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No, don't come here, Emporio.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.90,0:10:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,We're trapped in an\Nincident from the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.78,0:10:11.70,Default,,0,0,0,,This crash is already predetermined.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.78,0:10:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The only way to survive it is to escape\Nfrom the cockpit, but I have no idea how.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.68,0:10:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.74,0:10:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,We ain't gonna make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.82,0:10:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,We're out of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.84,0:10:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,There's less than a minute remaining,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.18,0:10:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and the fighter jet Jolene's\Non is gonna crash even sooner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.36,0:10:29.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.27,0:10:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.24,0:10:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, the jet fighter didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.30,0:10:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You're absolutely right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.94,0:10:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It didn't blow up, Emporio.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.52,0:10:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though I crashed the jet\Ninto the plane, it didn't explode.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.88,0:10:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way it would.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.20,0:10:46.64,Default,,0,0,0,,If it crashes into the ground in the past,\Nthen it won't blow up until that happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.72,0:10:50.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Until then, no matter what you do,\Nneither of the planes will explode.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.34,0:10:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yo, Jolene. I'm back.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.24,0:10:56.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Emporio, help me figure out\Nwhat to do next. Let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.58,0:11:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,In a miraculous turn of events six\Nyears ago on flight 2882 to Dallas,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.22,0:11:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,two of the passengers survived somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.42,0:11:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm looking the story up right\Nnow on my ghost computer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.40,0:11:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You need to get to their seats!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.42,0:11:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Escaping from that airplane is impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.80,0:11:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,But if this is really an event\Nthat occurred in the past,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.26,0:11:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,you should be able to survive\Nif you sit in those seats!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.90,0:11:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry, Emporio!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.04,0:11:19.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Find out which seats they are!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.06,0:11:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's Jolene Cujoh for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.56,0:11:25.40,Default,,0,0,0,,She always figures out a\Nway to create her own path.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.48,0:11:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then, do you think you're capable\Nof getting the job done, huh, Versus?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.76,0:11:31.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut your mouth!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.20,0:11:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Who the fuck do you think you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.64,0:11:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Found it, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.96,0:11:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,An old newspaper recorded\Nthe seats that the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.88,0:11:42.98,Default,,0,0,0,,survivors were sitting in\Nat the time of the crash.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.06,0:11:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like they're an economy class.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.26,0:11:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Seats 51D and 51F.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.62,0:11:48.90,Default,,0,0,0,,They're all the way in the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.98,0:11:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and you should know they weren't lying\Nabout the time of the crash being 2133.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.96,0:11:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the truth!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.87,0:11:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Run, Julie, run!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.72,0:11:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The enemy's inside the plane with us!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.96,0:12:00.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He's trying to get to\Nthose seats before we do!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.14,0:12:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants to destroy them so we can't sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.20,0:12:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,32 seconds until impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.18,0:12:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not that big of a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.12,0:12:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Just prevent them from sitting.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.42,0:12:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Doing so will bring about their end.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.46,0:12:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hermes, we need to protect the seats!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.62,0:12:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,If we can save those seats and make it\Nout of the plane crash in one piece,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.92,0:12:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,we should be able to\Nconfront the stand user!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.68,0:12:28.14,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to survive, so we can beat\Nthe living shit out of the user himself!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.22,0:12:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I couldn't destroy the\Nseats, but you'll never sit there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.58,0:12:33.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You have just 21 more seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.18,0:12:38.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, I repeat, you can sit in\Nseats 51D and 51F, but only those two.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.98,0:12:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not try to sit in any other seat!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.68,0:12:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,According to the records,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.14,0:12:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,all of the other seats were blown away\Nwhen the plane crashed and exploded!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.68,0:12:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Luckily,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.59,0:12:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,those two seats endured because the impact\Ncreated a quantum vacuum around them,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.98,0:12:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,so they're safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.89,0:12:54.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, sit down, make\Nsure you fasten your seatbelts!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.96,0:12:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,And protect yourselves with your\Nstands, otherwise you won't make it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.48,0:13:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Move it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.32,0:13:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna take this seat from you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.16,0:13:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what are you doing to me? Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.96,0:13:09.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of my way!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.08,0:13:11.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You guys aren't even actually real!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.16,0:13:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just records of who survived!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.04,0:13:15.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You aren't humans or\Nsome kind of lost souls!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.66,0:13:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The actual survivors aren't\Nliving their life right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.54,0:13:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,So stay point!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.96,0:13:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, it's time!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.16,0:13:22.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Fasten your seat back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.96,0:13:37.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, hey kid! Move it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.22,0:13:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Why the hell are you\Nsitting in those seats?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.18,0:13:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a sec, Hermes!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.72,0:13:50.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait what's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.32,0:13:52.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you two?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.32,0:13:54.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think I'm in my room anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.92,0:13:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,But where am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.38,0:14:00.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to change my bandages then\NI have to take medicine after my nap.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.54,0:14:03.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you two rats fall from the ceiling?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.22,0:14:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Nah that can't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.02,0:14:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,This isn't good. They're not.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.84,0:14:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Memories of passengers and we're\Ndefinitely not hallucinating.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.08,0:14:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey uh when is the nurse gonna be here?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.98,0:14:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,We're actually real kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.98,0:14:18.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That son of a bitch!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.36,0:14:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Versus must have grabbed\Nthese kids from the
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.06,0:14:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,hospital and pushed them\Ndown into the hole above us.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.40,0:14:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh there's no longer a need\Nto destroy those seats.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.46,0:14:31.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene Kujo don't forget\Nto fasten your seat belt.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.04,0:14:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Now go ahead and toss those brats.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.66,0:14:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,aside and take your seats.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.26,0:14:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,In that way, the two of you will\Nsurvive the crash and your sorry lives
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.92,0:14:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,will be spared.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.83,0:14:45.15,Default,,0,0,0,,But by the time you climb out of\Nthe wreckage of the crashed plane,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.24,0:14:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll be left with the crushing\Nweight of guilt on your conscience.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.58,0:14:50.52,Default,,0,0,0,,The guilt of sacrificing innocent
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.16,0:14:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,children so you can live another day.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.14,0:14:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you would have to\Ncome face me head on,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.56,0:14:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,carrying that guilt as a\Nconstant reminder of your choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.68,0:15:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Would anyone in a position like\Nthat have the fight Left in them to
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.58,0:15:06.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep going. My stand, Netherworld\Nisn't the strongest when it comes to
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.90,0:15:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,fighting abilities but with your\Nguilty conscience and broken spirit
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.66,0:15:14.30,Default,,0,0,0,,it's more than powerful enough to\Nsnuff out your life hey you there
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.38,0:15:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,jolene what are you guys doing\Nover there tell me what's happening
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.74,0:15:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,who's that person you're talking to\Ndamn it yo the plane's rocking back
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.40,0:15:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and forth jolene we have to grab\Nthe kids and sit two to a seat we
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.96,0:15:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't we'll all die that way?\NThere's only space for one person!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.80,0:15:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, we have three\Nkids to think about!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.90,0:15:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, ma 'am, are these your seats?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.20,0:15:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I'm not exactly very good at\Nstanding up by myself, but I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.90,0:15:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll move out of your\Nway, so please sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.58,0:15:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The time's come.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.00,0:15:48.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Two seconds till impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.66,0:15:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,One second.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.10,0:15:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,And now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.24,0:15:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,July!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.24,0:16:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It appears that you have defeated them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.62,0:16:22.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Good work, Versus.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.98,0:16:25.57,Default,,0,0,0,,But you sent three\Nchildren onto that plane.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.70,0:16:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,That was one extra kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.20,0:16:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you not feel even a little guilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.38,0:16:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,For what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.52,0:16:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It wasn't my fault that happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.66,0:16:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It was all because Jolene made contact\Nwith her friend over the radio.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.66,0:16:40.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It was them who found the\Nsurvivor's seat numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.62,0:16:43.90,Default,,0,0,0,,And also, remember who it\Nis I did all of this for.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.22,0:16:45.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You, Father Poochie.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.38,0:16:49.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Versus, look there.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.26,0:16:59.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That sticker it belongs to Hermes
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.78,0:17:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It's on the old man who survived\Nthe fact that he is still
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.36,0:17:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,with us means that no matter\Nwhat Happens the survivors won't
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.78,0:17:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,die and sing us how that's\NHermes's sticker using its special
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.96,0:17:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,ability She duplicated the\Nsurvivors and hid the child inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.42,0:17:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Where'd Ermes go?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.18,0:17:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.60,0:17:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene's gone too!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.96,0:17:28.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.40,0:17:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is Ermes?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.74,0:17:36.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Ermes!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.24,0:17:40.24,Default,,0,0,0,,She hid herself in the body\Nof the female survivor!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.50,0:17:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit! Er... Ermes!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.04,0:17:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,But that means Jolene is dead for sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.28,0:17:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way Jolene could have\Nfound a way to escape that explosion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.00,0:17:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,If I were in your position,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.80,0:17:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't allow such simple-minded\Nthoughts to cloud my judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.16,0:17:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Asshole.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.07,0:17:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly whose side are you on?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.52,0:18:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene unraveled as much of her\Nbody as she could into threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.92,0:18:21.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Then she hid inside of my body so she could\Nprotect herself against the collision.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.40,0:18:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good freaking grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.52,0:18:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene Kujo wasn't consumed by\Nguilt like you were expecting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.20,0:18:32.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, she's coming at you angrier than\Never with a righteous sense of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.48,0:18:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,What will you do now, Versus?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.08,0:18:37.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Another world!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.18,0:18:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You're done excavating\Nincidents from the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.90,0:18:52.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't let you dig up the\Nground's memories anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.44,0:18:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And now we finally got\Nyou backed into a corner.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.90,0:18:56.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You lose, poochie.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.88,0:18:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you want me to take\Ncare of this holy bastard?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.66,0:19:02.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't we going to finish this\Nworthless ass off together?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.94,0:19:04.44,Default,,0,0,0,,How unfortunate, Versus.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.66,0:19:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems as though you\Nhave lost this battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.86,0:19:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,By successfully bringing\Nherself closer to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.70,0:19:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene proved her destiny\Nis stronger than yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.56,0:19:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Go get him, Jolene!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.36,0:19:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to finish that fucking\Nasshole off already!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.76,0:19:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.56,0:19:31.91,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.12,0:19:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.72,0:19:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Jolene, kill his\Nass before he gets away!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.30,0:19:38.59,Default,,0,0,0,,When did you steal it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.76,0:19:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Was it just now when you got\Nblown away by Jolene's punch?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.32,0:19:42.84,Default,,0,0,0,,you must return it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.08,0:19:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hand it to me quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.84,0:19:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You cannot comprehend the\Nforces with which you're
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.52,0:19:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,meddling in.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.43,0:19:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't know about you,\Nbut I'm not dying here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.80,0:19:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Father Pucci.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.71,0:19:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Definitely not
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.26,0:19:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,when I've just gained control\Nover my very own abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.88,0:20:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Until now, I've spent my life in\Nshame and unable to stand up straight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.68,0:20:02.72,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way I'm\Ngonna die when I finally
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.80,0:20:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,understand why I was born into this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.68,0:20:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't understand a\Nsingle solitary thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.50,0:20:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It is imperative that That man\Ndoes not retrieve his memory,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.62,0:20:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,at least not for another three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.82,0:20:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't care, I'm not dying like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.86,0:20:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I still have a right to live\Na happy life too, don't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.84,0:20:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that supposed to mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.06,0:20:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell are you guys talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.54,0:20:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, forget about all that crazy\Nshit and just killed the fucker.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.88,0:20:26.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It's pointless to even try.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.86,0:20:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You two won't be able to kill me anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.96,0:20:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,He's going to get his memory back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.90,0:20:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I know this because I just\Nread the contents of his disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.64,0:20:37.56,Default,,0,0,0,,And when he does regain his memories, your\Nso-called friend will not be your ally.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.64,0:20:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Memory?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.64,0:20:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you mean Weather Forecast?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.86,0:20:42.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Was it his disc that you just threw?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.18,0:20:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Getting his memory stolen and\Nbeing thrown in prison aren't the
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.06,0:20:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,only misfortunes that poor Weather\NForecast has had to deal with.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.72,0:20:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He doesn't even remember how to use\Nhis stand to its fullest potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.70,0:20:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Unable to access the\Nforbidden power which his
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.04,0:20:59.04,Default,,0,0,0,,brother Poochie thought he\Nhad sealed away forever!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.00,0:21:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Because Weather happens to be\Nthe priest's biological brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.44,0:21:06.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Could it be that Rikyo was actually\Ntelling us the truth before?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.20,0:21:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast and the priest!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.82,0:21:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I see,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.86,0:21:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,so you had already used your netherworld
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.58,0:21:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,to read the secrets\Nheld in his memory disk.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.26,0:21:15.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Versus!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.17,0:21:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You insignificant piece\Nof refuse and scum!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.00,0:21:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't think that you can\Ninvade upon the fortress
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.98,0:21:22.45,Default,,0,0,0,,that Lord Danny have carefully cultivated!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.06,0:21:27.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you finally remember everything\Nnow, Pucci? Look up there. It's coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.20,0:21:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Those rainbows.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.64,0:21:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at them all!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.78,0:21:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It's heavy. Forecast!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.12,0:21:35.68,Default,,0,0,0,,The Devil's Rainbow!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.80,0:21:39.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather, what's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.44,0:21:40.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Which way is Jolene?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.86,0:21:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And why are you keeled over?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.14,0:21:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather, what's your deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.30,0:21:49.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.72,0:21:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,What was that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.36,0:21:57.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Yo, answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.82,0:21:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I was sitting in that seat, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.04,0:22:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Get your disgusting hands\Noff me, you asshole!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.34,0:22:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll kill you!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.12,0:22:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, oh, oh, oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.12,0:22:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,with hope of some
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.72,0:22:43.76,Default,,0,0,0,,place other than here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.12,0:22:50.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I smile
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.20,0:22:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,inside and all the while,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.06,0:23:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering about my destiny!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.96,0:23:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.96,0:23:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,about all
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.24,0:23:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,the things I'd like to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.92,0:23:29.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a dreamer,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.30,0:23:34.36,Default,,0,0,0,,a distant dreamer,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.44,0:23:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,dreaming far
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.30,0:23:44.50,Default,,0,0,0,,away from today.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.24,0:24:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,you Thank you.
